-- `EACH` is NOT a keyword (R-Q2: EACH is not a quantifier). It is recognised
-- only as the second word of the fork's join line `UPON EACH` (R-Q1, RULED
-- 2026-09-07), so a program may still use it as a name.

EACH MEANS 3

#EVAL EACH PLUS 1

GIVEN EACH IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
twice EACH MEANS EACH TIMES 2

#EVAL twice 4

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

-- ... and in the same file, the join line still reads as the fork
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign, and note each signature` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  FULFILLED
